# ACE Altius Consulting — Cursor Rules

## Project Overview
AI-powered visa and overseas education consultancy portal built for ACE Altius Consulting (Pakistan). Three user types: **Admin**, **Counselors**, and **Students/Clients**. Production at https://acevisa.vercel.app.

---

## Tech Stack
- **Framework**: Next.js 16 (App Router) — read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before writing Next.js code, APIs have breaking changes from older versions
- **Language**: TypeScript (strict)
- **Database**: Supabase (PostgreSQL)
- **Auth**: Supabase Auth + `@supabase/ssr` + custom middleware session control
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS v4 with custom design tokens
- **Icons**: `lucide-react`
- **Deployment**: Vercel

---

## Route Structure
```
src/app/
  (public)/          — Landing page, login, reset-password, schedule, chat (unauthenticated)
  (counselor)/       — /login, /dashboard/** (counselor-facing portal)
  (admin)/           — /admin/** (admin-facing portal)
  (student)/         — /portal/**, /student/** (client-facing portal)
```

Route groups use layouts for auth protection. Never skip the layout check.

---

## Authentication Rules

### Server-side (layouts, server components, API routes)
```ts
import { getAuthenticatedCounselor, requireAdmin } from '@/lib/supabase/server'

// In counselor layouts:
const counselor = await getAuthenticatedCounselor()
if (!counselor) redirect('/login')

// In admin layouts:
const admin = await requireAdmin() // handles redirect automatically
```

### Client-side
```ts
import { createClient } from '@/lib/supabase/client'
const supabase = createClient()
```

### Session / Remember Me
The app uses two custom cookies alongside Supabase's auth cookies:
- `ace_remember` — `'0'` or `'1'`, persistent 30 days, stores user's preference
- `ace_session_token` — session-only cookie (no maxAge), set only when `ace_remember=0`

The middleware (`src/middleware.ts`) enforces this: if `ace_remember=0` and `ace_session_token` is absent (browser was closed), it clears Supabase cookies and redirects to `/login`.

**Never bypass the middleware session check.**

### Clearing session cookies on sign-out
```ts
import { clearAceSessionCookies } from '@/lib/auth/session-cookies'
clearAceSessionCookies()
await supabase.auth.signOut()
```

---

## Supabase Patterns

### Server — always use admin client for DB reads in server components
```ts
import { createAdminClient } from '@/lib/supabase/server'
const supabase = createAdminClient() // uses SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
const { data } = await supabase.from('table').select('...')
```

### Client — use anon client for user-initiated mutations
```ts
const supabase = createClient()
await supabase.from('table').insert({...})
```

### Never expose `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` to the client. It is server-only.

### Key tables
| Table | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `counselors` | Staff accounts (role: `counselor` or `admin`) |
| `clients` | Student/client records |
| `meetings` | Scheduled meetings |
| `tasks` | Counselor tasks with due dates and completion tracking |
| `activity_logs` | Immutable audit trail — never delete rows |
| `deals` | CRM pipeline (service agreements) |
| `invoices` | Client invoices |
| `payments` | Payment records |
| `expenses` | Business expenses |
| `commission_rules` | Per-counselor commission rates |
| `notifications` | In-app notifications |
| `hr_flags` | HR negligence/escalation flags |

---

## Design System

### Color tokens — use these, never raw hex in components
```
bg       #E6E8E7   — page background (light stone)
text     #0A3F3A   — primary text / sidebar background (dark teal)
green    #B7C733   — accent / active nav (lime green)
orange   #E48328   — warnings, CTAs, sign-out
blue     #2083B9   — links, info states
black    #000000   — high-contrast text
```

Usage in Tailwind: `bg-bg`, `text-text`, `bg-green`, `text-orange`, `bg-blue`, etc.

### Logo usage rules
- **Always** wrap the logo in a white container when placed on a dark background (`bg-text`, `bg-[#0A3F3A]`, or any dark surface):
```tsx
<div className="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-white/95 px-2.5 py-1.5">
  <img src="/logo.png" alt="ACE Altius Consulting" className="h-9 w-auto" />
</div>
```
- Sizing: sidebar 36px (`h-9`), mobile header 28px (`h-7`), login/hero 64px (`h-16`)
- On light backgrounds (`bg-bg`), use the img directly without a container

### Icon contrast rule
Icons placed on the same-color background as themselves must use a contrasting color. For dark `bg-text` headers:
```tsx
// Wrong — invisible
<Bell className="text-[#0A3F3A]" />  // dark icon on dark bg

// Correct
<Bell className="text-white" />      // or text-bg
```
The `NotificationBell` component accepts `variant="dark"` for dark backgrounds.

### Touch targets — mobile accessibility
All interactive elements must meet 44×44px minimum:
```tsx
className="min-h-[44px] min-w-[44px]"
```

### Border radius
- Cards/modals: `rounded-[20px]` or `rounded-card`
- Buttons: `rounded-full` (pill) or `rounded-xl`
- Nav items: `rounded-xl`

---

## Component Conventions

### Client components — mark explicitly
```tsx
'use client'
```
Only use when you need: browser APIs, useState, useEffect, event handlers, useRouter.

### Server components — default
Layouts and pages are server components by default. Fetch data here, pass to client components as props.

### Forms
- Always use `type FormEvent` and `e.preventDefault()`
- Show loading state on submit button (`disabled={loading}`)
- Show inline error messages, never alert()

### Sidebar patterns
Both `DashboardSidebar` and `AdminSidebar` handle desktop + mobile with the same `SidebarContent` internal component. Mobile uses a slide-in overlay panel. When adding nav items, add to the `navItems` array only — don't add separate mobile/desktop markup.

---

## API Routes
- Located at `src/app/api/*/route.ts`
- Always validate the request body before using it
- Use `createAdminClient()` for DB access in API routes (server context)
- Return `NextResponse.json({ error: '...' }, { status: 4xx })` for errors

---

## PWA
- Manifest: `public/manifest.json`
- Service worker: `public/sw.js`
- Registration: `src/components/PWARegister.tsx` (client component, mounted in root layout)
- The service worker uses network-first for navigation and cache-first for static assets
- API routes (`/api/*`) are always fetched fresh — never cached in SW

---

## File & Naming Conventions
- Pages: `page.tsx` (default export, PascalCase component name)
- Layouts: `layout.tsx`
- Components: PascalCase filename, named export
- Utilities: camelCase filename
- All imports use `@/` alias for `src/`

---

## Things to Never Do
- Don't use `localStorage` or `sessionStorage` — the app uses cookie-based auth
- Don't call `supabase.auth.getSession()` for auth checks — use `getUser()` or the helper functions (sessions can be spoofed, users cannot)
- Don't delete rows from `activity_logs` — immutable audit trail
- Don't expose `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` outside server context
- Don't add nav items as raw JSX — use the `navItems` array in the sidebar components
- Don't hardcode hex colors in components — use the Tailwind design tokens
- Don't place a logo on a dark background without a white container
- Don't use `router.push` without also calling `router.refresh()` after auth state changes
